{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"91fb91cb53330920d8b57cd3637e3b2b5dca5703bb0bae660b23426db5b901be","digest":{"component_or_area":"AGENTS.md documentation","key_entities":["AGENTS.md","find_referencing_symbols","_anthropic_cache_settings","monkeypatch.setattr","tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py","runner.py","test_structured.py","docs/"],"problem_keywords":["documentation correctness","LSP limitations","symbol resolution","string literals","grep false positives","stale index"],"propositions":["AGENTS.md states an unconditional preference for LSP symbol tools over grep, but this claim is false when symbols are named as string literals (e.g., monkeypatch.setattr, getattr, importlib) which LSP cannot resolve","LSP find_referencing_symbols missed a call site that used monkeypatch.setattr with a string literal, causing an agent following the current rule exclusively to overlook a real reference","LSP index can lag behind recent edits in the working tree, reporting stale line numbers while grep on the working tree returns current positions","The current bare preference rule trains agents to discount it, contributing to navigation failures and missing references"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787356602278425001,"uuid":"c1101159-b1ac-4f0f-b723-a798acd6d351"}